    ],
    "findings": [
      {
        "body": "Gain 4, Work 2, Harm 3\nRaise: Functional.\nCase: normal use - a repo tests two Python apps with separate pytest commands, both apps have an unpackaged `tests/test_user.py`, and a change selects tests in both. The picker installs this plugin in each command (`src/forge/fasttest.py:141-144`), and this line adds every proof file to each invocation. Naming the first app's test makes the second invocation collect both `test_user.py` files. Pytest's default import mode requires those module names to be unique, so collection fails and close refuses an otherwise valid change. [Pytest documents this import behavior](https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#choosing-an-import-mode).",
        "file": "src/forge/fasttest.py",
        "gain": 4,
